{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Take heed to yourselves, lest your heart be deceived.</b> Through the ease and wealth that you will have in the land — do not turn aside from the way and cleave to idolatry, heaven forfend, and the anger of HaShem burn against you and He shut up the heaven so that there be no rain. And He mentioned this because idolaters think that through their worship rain comes and all the great ones of the earth prosper; therefore He informed them here that the heaven will be shut up when they serve idolatry and there will be no rain at all. And thus Isaiah, of blessed memory, mentioned (Isaiah 30:22): ״וטמאתם את צפוי פסילי כספך ואת אפודת מסכת זהבך תזרם כמו דוה צא תאמר לו״, and immediately after it: ״ונתן מטר זרעך אשר תזרע את האדמה״ and so on, and ״והיה דשן ושמן״ and so on — this comes to explain that the other upper forces do not bring rain, nor is there among the vanities of the nations any power to bring material sustenance, for HaShem our Elohim alone is He who brings rain, and to Him we look forward."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:32.054614976Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}